  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNITAR Fellowship Programme in Peacemaking and Preventive Diplomacy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Support to the UNITAR Fellowship Programme in Peacemaking and Preventive Diplomacy. The Fellowship Programme will offer advanced training in conflict analysis, negotiation and mediation to female and male international and national civil servants to deepen knowledge and strengthen skills in these areas. The programme will be based on the latest knowledge, with the primary focus on preventing and resolving international disputes through the United Nations. The strengthening of women&apos;s participation in peace processes are highly prioritised.

2. Support to UNITAR regional fellowship programme to enhance conflict prevention and peacemaking in Africa. It aims to contribute significantly to the continent&#x2019;s capacity for conflict prevention and peacemaking, as well as in strengthening the competence of African Member States and female and male staff from key regional/sub-regional organizations and peace missions in Africa in these areas.</narrative>
  </description>
